<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<dataModel xmlns="http://xmlns.oracle.com/oxp/xmlp" version="2.1"
           defaultDataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM">
  <!--
    DMT_BEN_BENFY_RECON_DM — BIP reconciliation report contract v1 for
    BenBeneficiary (Benefit beneficiary designations, loaded via HCM Data Loader).
    Design doc: "BIP reconciliation report contract - v1" (nine columns, six
    parameters, keyset pagination) plus its HDL note: "each HDL object gets a
    Contract v1 report whose rows are the BASE tier (key + Fusion id); its ERROR
    rows are optional because HDL failures arrive per-record in the HDL response
    and are tagged [FUSION_ERROR] before the report runs."

    BASE-TIER ONLY. An HDL load has no interface table, so this report returns the
    BASE tier: one row per migrated record that Fusion positively confirmed by
    writing a HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP entry, with the Fusion-assigned SURROGATE_ID
    as FUSION_ID. This is the same base-tier proof the Salaries and BenParticipant
    reconcilers use, and the design doc endorses it for HDL objects.

    HOW THIS OBJECT LOADS (DMT_BEN_BENFY_HDL_GEN_PKG, 2026-09-17 re-model):
      * Beneficiary designation is its own HDL business object: BeneficiaryEnrollment
        (parent) with the child component DesignateBeneficiary. The generator writes
        a BeneficiaryEnrollment.dat. The earlier model wrongly emitted a
        PersonBenefitBalance.dat (accumulated benefit balances, not designations)
        that collided on file name/discriminator with BenParticipant and BenDependent;
        this report reconciles against the CORRECT object, OBJECT_NAME =
        'BeneficiaryEnrollment'.
      * The parent BeneficiaryEnrollment component carries
        SourceSystemOwner = 'HRC_SQLLOADER' and
        SourceSystemId = (prefixed PERSON_NUMBER) || '_BENENRL'.
        That _BENENRL value is also the BenBeneficiary TFM row's RECON_KEY (one key
        definition per object).
      * On load Fusion records one HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP row per enrolled worker:
        OBJECT_NAME = 'BeneficiaryEnrollment',
        SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER = 'HRC_SQLLOADER',
        SOURCE_SYSTEM_ID = our _BENENRL key,
        SURROGATE_ID = the Fusion-assigned base-table id.
      This report filters to SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER='HRC_SQLLOADER' so Fusion-seeded
      rows (owner FUSION) are never counted.

    BASE TABLE / FUSION_ID — HONEST NOTE. Beneficiary designation lands in the
    Benefits (BEN_*) base tables. Those physical base tables are NOT selectable by
    name from the FSCM BIP reporting user (the same restriction the Salaries and
    BenParticipant reconcilers hit). HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP is therefore the
    authoritative, verifiable base-tier source, and its SURROGATE_ID is the Fusion
    base id we return as FUSION_ID — faithful to the design doc's HDL note (key +
    Fusion id via the key map).

    LIVE STATE ON THIS POD (verified 2026-09-20, fin_impl / ApplicationDB_FSCM):
      * OBJECT_NAME 'BeneficiaryEnrollment' has NO rows yet in
        HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP — beneficiary designation has not been re-loaded
        through the corrected generator on this pod.
      * The historical HRC_SQLLOADER beneficiary loads sit under the WRONG object
        OBJECT_NAME='PersonBenefitBalance' with the OLD suffix '_BENBNFY' (e.g.
        67936DMTBNFY001_BENBNFY -> SURROGATE_ID 300000331552758). Their SURROGATE_ID
        values are populated real Fusion base ids, which proves the map-row +
        SURROGATE_ID shape this report relies on; they are not counted here because
        this report targets the correct object and the new _BENENRL suffix.
      * Standalone shape and paging behaviour were validated best-effort against the
        structurally identical PersonBenefitBalance key rows (same nine columns, same
        keyset predicate) — see the PR body for the exact rows and the empty-page
        confirmation.

    NINE response columns, in contract order:
      OBJECT_TYPE, RECORD_KEY, SOURCE_TYPE('BASE'), FUSION_STATUS('SUCCESS'),
      FUSION_ID (SURROGATE_ID), ERROR_MESSAGE (NULL), LOAD_REQUEST_ID (NULL),
      SOURCE_REF (= SourceSystemId), DMT_REFERENCE (NULL).
    SIX parameters: P_RUN_ID, P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID, P_IMPORT_ESS_ID, P_PREFIX,
      P_CHUNK_SIZE, P_AFTER_KEY.
    KEYSET pagination by RECORD_KEY (P_AFTER_KEY cursor, P_CHUNK_SIZE page).
      LOAD_REQUEST_ID / P_IMPORT_ESS_ID do not survive into the base for an HDL
      load, so BASE-tier matching is by run prefix (P_PREFIX). LOAD_REQUEST_ID is
      returned NULL per the brief's column mapping.
  -->
  <dataProperties>
    <property name="include_parameters" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_null_Element" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_rowsettag" value="false"/>
    <property name="xml_tag_case" value="upper"/>
  </dataProperties>
  <dataSets>
    <dataSet name="ben_benfy_recon" type="complex">
      <sql dataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM"><![CDATA[
SELECT
    object_type, record_key, source_type, fusion_status,
    fusion_id, error_message, load_request_id, source_ref, dmt_reference
FROM (
    -- BASE tier: positive proof in the HCM integration key map. The HDL load
    -- writes one HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP row per enrolled worker
    -- (OBJECT_NAME='BeneficiaryEnrollment', SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER='HRC_SQLLOADER')
    -- whose SURROGATE_ID is the Fusion base id. One row per migrated enrollment.
    SELECT 'BenBeneficiary'               AS object_type,
           m.source_system_id             AS record_key,
           'BASE'                         AS source_type,
           'SUCCESS'                      AS fusion_status,
           MAX(m.surrogate_id)            AS fusion_id,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS error_message,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(30))     AS load_request_id,
           m.source_system_id             AS source_ref,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS dmt_reference
    FROM   hrc_integration_key_map m
    WHERE  m.object_name         = 'BeneficiaryEnrollment'
    AND    m.source_system_owner = 'HRC_SQLLOADER'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE :P_PREFIX || '%'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE '%\_BENENRL' ESCAPE '\'
    GROUP BY m.source_system_id
)
-- Keyset predicate. An empty P_AFTER_KEY (first page) binds to NULL in BIP, so
-- treat NULL as "from the start": every non-null RECORD_KEY sorts after the empty
-- string. On later pages P_AFTER_KEY carries the previous page's last RECORD_KEY
-- and only greater keys are returned.
WHERE  (:P_AFTER_KEY IS NULL OR record_key > :P_AFTER_KEY)
ORDER BY record_key
FETCH FIRST :P_CHUNK_SIZE ROWS ONLY
      ]]></sql>
    </dataSet>
  </dataSets>
  <output rootName="DATA_DS" uniqueRowName="false">
    <nodeList name="data-structure">
      <dataStructure tagName="DATA_DS">
        <group name="G_1" label="G_1" source="ben_benfy_recon">
          <element name="OBJECT_TYPE"     value="OBJECT_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="OBJECT_TYPE"/>
          <element name="RECORD_KEY"      value="RECORD_KEY"      dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="RECORD_KEY"/>
          <element name="SOURCE_TYPE"     value="SOURCE_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="SOURCE_TYPE"/>
          <element name="FUSION_STATUS"   value="FUSION_STATUS"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="FUSION_STATUS"/>
          <element name="FUSION_ID"       value="FUSION_ID"       dataType="xsd:integer" tagName="FUSION_ID"/>
          <element name="ERROR_MESSAGE"   value="ERROR_MESSAGE"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="ERROR_MESSAGE"/>
          <element name="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" value="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="LOAD_REQUEST_ID"/>
          <element name="SOURCE_REF"      value="SOURCE_REF"      dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="SOURCE_REF"/>
          <element name="DMT_REFERENCE"   value="DMT_REFERENCE"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="DMT_REFERENCE"/>
        </group>
      </dataStructure>
    </nodeList>
  </output>
  <eventTriggers/>
  <lexicals/>
  <parameters>
    <parameter name="P_RUN_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_RUN_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_PREFIX" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_PREFIX" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <!-- Keyset pagination: page size + cursor. The reconciler calls with an empty
         P_AFTER_KEY first, then passes the last RECORD_KEY received on each next
         call, until a short page returns. -->
    <parameter name="P_CHUNK_SIZE" dataType="integer" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_CHUNK_SIZE" defaultValue="5000" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_AFTER_KEY" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_AFTER_KEY" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
  </parameters>
  <valueSets/>
  <bursting/>
</dataModel>
